# v0.1.2 item 6 — loam-amend ergonomics sweep

2026-05-03. v0.1.2 item per `docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-x-roadmap.md`
§2 v0.1.2 item 6 + §8 method-decision register backfill.

Sub-plan: `docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-2-loam-amend-ergonomics.md`.

FIDRAFT entries closed (`docs/rebuild/FUTURE_IDEAS_DRAFT.md` —
all 2026-05-03 captures from main session):
  - "`loam amend apply` does not commit the apply step BY DESIGN"
  - "`loam amend seal` requires clean working tree — stash-then-pop
    workaround used in every FBE.x"
  - "`loam amend apply` partner-prefix derivation bug — derives
    from name field assuming framework/<name>/+ bare-<name>/
    shapes; misses plugins/<name>/ shaped components"

Scope (per sub-plan §4): single-component fence on
`plugins/dev-sdlc/`. The dev-sdlc plugin's seal-test fences
`plugins/dev-sdlc/tools/loam-amend/` along with the rest of the
plugin. Three AC families:

  - AC.LAE.1 — `loam amend apply` (non-dry-run) auto-commits the
    apply step. Stages per-component seal_test + sidecar paths;
    authors a deterministic `chore(amend): <description> apply —
    <comp-list> BASELINE+sidecar bump to <baseline-short>` commit.
    Co-Authored-By trailer mirrors seal.py's `_claude_environment()`.
    Idempotent re-runs with no on-disk change skip the commit.
    Commit failure halts with operator-actionable diagnostic +
    exit 3.

  - AC.LAE.2 — `loam amend seal --allow-untracked-globs <pattern>`
    flag (repeatable) admits dirty paths matching the named glob
    via `fnmatch.fnmatchcase`. Patterns are dirty-check-only;
    NOT staged or committed. Patterns are anchored at the repo
    root (no implicit trailing `*`). Common case:
    `--allow-untracked-globs docs/rebuild/FUTURE_IDEAS_DRAFT.md`
    for in-flight capture state.

  - AC.LAE.3 — `loam amend apply` partner-prefix derivation now
    reads from the manifest's `seal_test` path (canonical
    shape-discriminator) rather than the `name` field. Fixes the
    latent `plugins/<name>/`-located component mis-shape.
    Defensive fallbacks preserve back-compat with
    framework-located + legacy 3-segment fixture seal_test paths.

  - AC.LAE.S — single-component fence on `plugins/dev-sdlc/`;
    plus `docs/rebuild/plans/` via universal prefix.

Smokes captured pre-seal (verbatim):

    === Smoke A (AC.LAE.1 — auto-commit) ===
    applied:
      - comp: BASELINE → 076223b...
      - comp: SEAL_COMMIT → 076223b...
    committed: 86d63ba (apply auto-commit)
    Last commit subject: "chore(amend): smoke-a apply — comp
    BASELINE+sidecar bump to 076223b"
    Body carries: amendment-#99 reference, sub-plan reference,
    per-change list, mechanised-by note, Co-Authored-By trailer
    (under CLAUDECODE=1).

    === Smoke B (AC.LAE.2 — --allow-untracked-globs) ===
    Without flag:
      HALT: dirty-working-tree
      working tree carries unrelated dirty paths:
        ?? docs/
      Refusing to seal.
    With --allow-untracked-globs 'docs/rebuild/FUTURE_IDEAS_DRAFT.md'
    --allow-untracked-globs 'docs/':
      sealed: chore(seals): smoke-a — comp at 86d63ba
    Post-seal: docs/ remains untracked (admission was dirty-check-
    only; not staged).

    === Smoke C (AC.LAE.3 — partner-prefix from seal_test) ===
    Mixed-fence amendment with framework/alpha/ + plugins/beta/:
      alpha: allowed_prefixes += ['plugins/beta/']
      beta: allowed_prefixes += ['framework/alpha/']
    alpha test file post-apply carries `"plugins/beta/"` (correct
    shape; NOT the buggy `framework/beta/` or bare `beta/`).
    beta test file post-apply carries `"framework/alpha/"`.

    === Smoke D (loam-amend test suite — touched-only) ===
    183 passed in ~40s.

    === Smoke E (dev-sdlc sealed-component sweep) ===
    48 passed in ~1s.

All ACs (AC.LAE.{1,2,3}) pass: auto-commit lands with conventional
shape; --allow-untracked-globs admits glob-matched dirt without
staging; partner-prefix derives from seal_test path correctly
across framework/ + plugins/ + mixed shapes.

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - Auto-commit subject shape `chore(amend): <desc> apply —
    <comp-list> BASELINE+sidecar bump to <baseline-short>` mirrors
    the manual apply commits authored by recent agents (e.g.
    `8cbab6a` for v0.1.2 item 5) for audit-trail consistency.
  - Auto-commit body sections: amendment-number reference, sub-
    plan reference, per-component change list, mechanised-by
    note, Co-Authored-By trailer (under Claude env).
  - Stage-explicit (per-component seal_test + sidecar paths from
    manifest). Avoid `git add -A` — could pick up unrelated
    dirty state if operator's tree is dirty. Mirrors seal.py's
    paths_to_stage pattern.
  - Co-Authored-By detection re-implements `_claude_environment()`
    helper in apply.py rather than re-importing from seal.py
    (smaller import surface; both helpers track the same env-var
    list `_CLAUDE_ENV_VARS`).
  - `fnmatch.fnmatchcase` for glob matching — standard library,
    case-sensitive (POSIX-shell convention), no shape-magic.
  - `--allow-untracked-globs` patterns anchored at repo root:
    `docs/rebuild/FUTURE_IDEAS_DRAFT.md` matches the literal file;
    `docs/rebuild/*` matches direct children only; `docs/**/*` is
    the recursive form. Documented in --help.
  - `--allow-untracked-globs` admission is dirty-check-only —
    patterns are NOT staged or committed. The seal step still
    only stages declared sidecars + narrative + plan-doc per
    existing logic.
  - Partner-prefix helper `_partner_prefix(seal_test, name)`
    parses 4-segment `<base>/<name>/tests/<file>.py` shape →
    `<base>/<name>/`. 3-segment legacy `<name>/tests/<file>.py`
    shape → `<name>/`. Defensive fallback to `framework/<name>/`
    for any non-canonical seal_test. Self-exclusion in widening
    uses the same derivation.

Out of scope (per sub-plan §8):

  - Manifest-level `allow_untracked_globs` admission — deferred;
    CLI flag covers immediate workflow. Manifest field can land
    later if observed pain-point recurs.
  - Updating in-flight dispatch prompts that say "manually create
    the apply commit" — out of fence. Backwards-compat per
    sub-plan Surface #2 / Outcome A: manual commits become
    no-ops on top of the auto-commit; harmless.
  - Migrating prior manifests' `extra_allowed_prefixes` to drop
    now-redundant `<name>/` bare admissions — out of fence;
    opportunistic cleanup at next touch.

